# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: RISC3D, the 3D driver interface.
Package: RISC3D
Section: System
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32
Components: Resources.!RISC3D (Movable)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-risc3d
Description: RISC OS's 3D driver interface, so Mesa programs use the GPU
 !RISC3D lets programs that draw with riscos-mesa (OpenGL, OpenGL ES)
 use the machine's GPU: the RISC3D module, with GPU drivers for a
 Raspberry Pi 4, 400 or CM4 (V3DRender) and RISC OS on Linux (Linux3D).
 Each driver starts only on its own machine; elsewhere programs draw in
 software as before. It goes in !Boot.Resources and loads at start-up.
Build-Map: !RISC3D -> Resources/!RISC3D
Build-Notice: RISC3D, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-risc3d/releases
 .
 RISC3D and Linux3D are Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Youll, under the MIT
 licence (at the end of !RISC3D.!Help). V3DRender is Copyright (c) 2026
 Andrew Youll and others, under the GNU GPL version 2 or later; its
 source is at https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-v3drender. The notices
 follow.
Build-Copyright: !RISC3D/!Help
